	<div class="smittenkitchen-print-hide">
			</div>

	Twenty years ago, I started this website because I wanted a place to share recipes I was excited about, as it&#8217;s practically coded into my DNA to be an unfettered yap about the things I love. [<a href="https://x.com/sadderlizards/status/2002813306869067805">This is me.</a>] The larger context was that upon reaching so-called adulthood, I&#8217;d found that while I knew how to cook, there were still so many things I hadn’t figured out, such as: how to turn a can of tomatoes into not just an okay pasta sauce, but <a href="https://smittenkitchen.com/2010/01/tomato-sauce-with-butter-and-onions/">a spectacular one</a>; how to make <a href="https://smittenkitchen.com/2016/02/everyday-meatballs/">really good meatballs</a>; perfect <a href="https://smittenkitchen.com/2013/01/ethereally-smooth-hummus/">hummus</a>; and a <a href="https://smittenkitchen.com/2024/04/new-york-crumb-cake/">crumb cake</a> I’d want to make forever.</p>
